::ENG4_U06_L08_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.C.01] Unit 6 synthesis scenario: A final project about career certification access must include oral explanation, digital slides, research support, multimedia publication, source credits, and an audience-ready sharing format. Which option best synthesizes oral, digital, and multimedia communication? {
~A. Treat the speech, slides, and publication as unrelated products.#Incorrect. This separates connected communication tasks. Unit 6 synthesis requires the oral claim, digital design, evidence, and publication format to work together for one audience purpose.
=B. Use a focused oral claim, accessible slides, credited evidence, and a publication format that fits the audience.#Correct. This answer best applies Unit 6 communication skills with clear reasoning, evidence, audience awareness, and publication readiness.
~C. Add more information to every slide so the presentation seems complete.#Incorrect. More slide text can reduce clarity. Effective digital communication selects the evidence the audience needs and explains extra detail through speaker notes or narration.
~D. Ignore source credits if the final product looks polished.#Incorrect. Polish cannot replace credibility. Publication-ready communication must credit borrowed facts, ideas, and media so the audience can trust the work.
}

